  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: S01, S02 Received 08 December 2022; 03.01 Rev C, 03.02 Rev C Received 16 February 2023.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to first occupation of the hereby approved development full details of the arrangements for the storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 5 - Secure covered cycle parking facilities (for not less than 4 bicycles) for the occupants of the development shall be installed in at the front of the property. The approved facilities shall conform to the current Westtrans West London Cycle Parking Guidance (or such other guidance as shall supersede it) in design and layout and be fully implemented and made available for use before the first occupation of the development or commencement of the approved use as appropriate and thereafter retained for use at all times without obstruction.",
    "Condition : 6 - Before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, the existing vehicular access to 42 North Drive TW3 1PU shall be permanently closed and kerbs and footway reinstated so that it cannot be used as an access across the pavement.",
    "Condition : 7 - Prior to first occupation of the building(s) hereby approved, the development shall have been constructed to achieve an internal water use of 105 litres/person/day or less.",
    "Condition : 8 - A. Notwithstanding the approved details, no development above ground level shall take place until an Energy Strategy is submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The strategy shall demonstrate how the proposed development would achieve 'Zero Carbon'. Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.\r\nB. Prior to commencement of development the applicant shall have entered into a formal agreement with the Council to make an agreed contribution to the Council's Carbon Offset Fund, in accordance with the Energy Strategy agreed under part A of this condition.",
    "Condition : 9 - The rear garden shall be sub-divided as shown on the plan drawing numbered 03.01 Rev C and thereafter maintained as such for the duration of the development hereby permitted."
  ],
